  "result": "Done! I've added payment terms support to invoices:\n\n**Updated createInvoice:**\n- Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Valid terms: 'NET14', 'NET30', 'EOM'\n- Calculates and stores `dueDate` based on terms:\n  - NET14: issueDate + 14 days\n  - NET30: issueDate + 30 days\n  - EOM: last day of issue month\n- Stores both `terms` and `dueDate` on invoice\n\n**Added helper function:**\n- `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` - Calculates due date\n  - Handles month boundaries correctly\n  - Proper leap year support (Feb 28/29)\n  - Uses UTC consistently\n\n**Added error code:**\n- TERMS_INVALID: \"Payment terms must be 'NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM'.\"\n\n**Tests added:** 8 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Default NET30 behavior (Jan 15 \u2192 Feb 14)\n- NET14 calculation (Jan 15 \u2192 Jan 29)\n- EOM for various months (Jan, Apr, Feb leap/non-leap)\n- Invalid terms rejection\n- Month boundary handling (Jan 20 + 30 \u2192 Feb 19)\n\n**All 141 tests pass** \u2713",
